  "why": "The two arms that reported a failure and a wall time far above every other arm were measured with the process running as uid 0. The proof is in those arms' own logs: integrations/dsh-director/test/memory-vector.test.mjs test 9 (r30) fails with EISDIR on unlink '<vfile>.filter-blocked', and its fixture only creates that path as a DIRECTORY when process.getuid() === 0 (blockFilter: mkdirSync for root, chmod 0o400 otherwise). The suite branches on the uid, so a root arm measures a shape the gate never uses: core/repository_executor.py:896 runs every node command with --user os.getuid():os.getgid(), and the backend process is uid 1000."
